sigil_soc_top on sky130hd: whole-SoC hierarchical place and route, #11 (2026-10-22/23)
======================================================================================

STATUS: GDS generated / place-and-route complete -- not taped out.

The whole Sigil SoC -- in-house RV64GCV core with the element-serial vector
unit, FPU and 4 KiB L1 I$/D$ (7 OpenRAM macros), the crypto/hash engine
(SHA-256/512, Keccak, EC field unit) and the SoC glue (reset synchronizer,
fabric, CLINT, PLIC, UART, boot ROM, crypto bridge) -- placed and routed on
sky130hd with OpenROAD-flow-scripts as a hierarchical design on a
non-Caravel die. RTL unchanged (sky130 configuration SIGIL_SRAM_SKY130 +
SIGIL_SOC_PARAMS_SKY130). No IO pad ring, no seal ring: SoC signals are
die-edge pins.

  branch   11-sky130-hier; top config flow/designs/sky130hd/sigil_hier/
           (its floorplan defaults since commit 43f30cd = this run),
           hard blocks sigil_hier/sigil_cpu/ and sigil_hier/sigil_crypto_top/,
