  - Blocks route met1-met4 and export their met4 VDD/VSS straps as pins;
    the top-level met5 stripes (1.6 um, 27.2 um pitch) cross both blocks
    and drop via4 onto them (pdn.tcl, -grid_over_boundary block grid). The
    glue column has the platform grid (met1 rails, met4 / met5 stripes).
  - Top-level synthesis reads port-only block stubs (stubs/; ORFS BLOCKS
    fails on sigil_cpu's parameters under yosys-slang); every later stage
    reads the block abstracts (sigil_cpu.lef, sigil_crypto_top.lef) and
    their TT timing models.
  - Why 15.8 mm^2 rather than ~14: the blocks alone are 14.28 mm^2 (the
    CPU block needed 3400 x 3420 to route), and the glue column must be
    ~300 um wide. Block x position swept with the final blocks:
    x = 200 (die 3610 wide) 48,973 overflowed global-route gcells
    (stopped); x = 255: 134 (still detail-routed to 0); x = 305: 0;
    x = 405: 0.

