STATIC TIMING (OpenSTA, 40 ns, OpenRCX SPEF of each level)
----------------------------------------------------------
  corner_sta.tcl per level and corner; the top level reads the blocks'
  per-corner timing models (write_timing_model of the routed blocks,
  BLOCK_LIBS), so its paths include the block I/O arcs. Block "internal" =
  register / macro endpoints in the block (the block-level checks of its
  output ports against the 12 ns boundary budget are replaced, at SoC
  level, by the real top-level paths). Every corner uses the platform's
  only (typical) RC extraction rules; the OpenRAM macros only have a TT
  model and keep TT timing in all corners. Full summaries: sta/.

