KLAYOUT DRC
-----------
  Deck: signoff/sky130hd_sigil.lydrc = the image's ORFS sky130hd deck
  (platforms/sky130hd/drc/sky130hd.lydrc) with FEOL switched on (stock:
  BEOL + OFFGRID only; 381 rule categories in all) and tiled instead of
  deep processing (200 um tiles, 5 um borders, 16 threads); the rules are
  unchanged. Deep mode ran single-threaded for hours on single rules of
  this layout (and tiling costs the same per mm^2 for 40-1000 um tiles);
  what made the earlier block-level runs slow was the OpenRAM content:
  a 300 x 300 um window of a VRF macro holds 3.8M li polygons (14x a
  std-cell window) and li.3 alone did not finish there in 10 min.
  So the merged GDS is checked in two parts that together cover it:

  1. Merged final GDS (6_final.gds of t2e, blocks merged in) with the
     OpenRAM macro cells left out (-rd exclude=sky130_sram_*): 1 h 42 min,
     24 GB. 8 markers, 1 class:
        8  m2.1  min. m2 width 0.14 um   (all in the CPU block)
     They sit at 4 places where a router m2 jog of sigil_cpu lands on an
     OpenRAM dff pin pad (2 x 1 marker edge pair each; die um ~(947.9,
     2754.1) on the I$ data macro, (2793.8 / 2805.5 / 2863.9, 938.7) on
     a VRF macro): the two router rectangles touch over 0.07 x 0.07 um,
     and the macro's 0.33 x 0.26 um m2 pad covers that junction. With
     the macro content included (same deck, flat, windows around the 4
     sites) there is no m2.1 marker at those places; the remaining
     markers in the windows are OpenRAM-internal or slivers made by the
     window clipping. OpenROAD's DRT (macro LEF obstructions) reported 0.
     drc/t2e_merged_drc_summary.txt (+ shapes at the sites),
     drc/t2e-nosram_drc.lyrdb.gz.

  2. The OpenRAM macros (platform sky130ram GDS, the cells merged into
     sigil_cpu), each standalone, same deck, tiled 100 um: flat marker
     counts per macro, x instances in the SoC (2 x 44x64, 3 x 64x256,
     2 x 128x256):
        44x64 610,998; 64x256 3,411,963; 128x256 6,759,168
        -> 24,976,221 in the SoC, 37 classes; largest li.3 4,785,571,
        difftap.2 2,963,628, licon.5 2,474,120, licon.11a 2,458,204,
        m1.4 2,248,514, licon.15 1,367,629, poly.8 1,112,858 ... psdm.1 14
        (full table: drc/openram_macros_drc_summary.txt)
     The deck has no SRAM-core rules (no areaid.ce exemptions, no
     bit-cell rule set), so the bit-cell arrays and OpenRAM periphery
     cells are measured against logic rules; these macros are the
     OpenRAM blocks shipped with ORFS, used unmodified. (Stock deep mode
     on the 44x64 macro: 159,037 hierarchical markers, the same 37
     classes; on the larger two it spent 2 h on one FEOL rule and was
     stopped.)

  Total for the merged GDS: 24,976,229 markers in 38 classes (the 37
  OpenRAM classes + m2.1); outside the OpenRAM macros 8, none of which
  remains with the macro shapes present. For comparison, the nangate45
  GDS (2026-10-21) reported 179 KLayout markers with the FreePDK45 deck.
  Not covered by KLayout: interactions between the routing next to a
  macro and the macro's internal shapes other than at the 4 sites above
  (checked by OpenROAD's DRT against the macros' LEF obstructions: 0).

