REPRODUCE
---------
  Host wrappers in host_scripts/ (sigil-sky130: ~/sigil = branch
  checkout, ~/sb = work dir; run.sh runs make in the pinned image on a
  git-archive snapshot of a commit, so later commits do not change a
  run). Inside the image every step is plain ORFS make:
    make DESIGN_CONFIG=designs/sky130hd/<cfg> NUM_CORES=<n> <vars> <target>

  1. Blocks: CPU s116 -> s116d and crypto w34m, commands in
     ../w7-sky130-hier-2026-10-22.log ("Reproduce" of each block); their
     results (LEF, typ lib, GDS) are read from
     results/sky130hd/sigil_hier_<block>/<variant>/; per-corner block
     models: corner_sta.tcl MODEL=1 (~/sb/sta/cpu-s116d, crypto-w34m).
  2. Top level t2 (snapshot a27e98f; its floorplan arguments are the
     config defaults since 43f30cd), host_scripts/trun.sh:
       FP='DIE_AREA="0 0 3715 4260" CORE_AREA="2 2 3713 4258" SIGIL_CPU_XY="305 10" SIGIL_CRYPTO_XY="305 3470"'
       B="SIGIL_CPU_VARIANT=s116d SIGIL_CRYPTO_VARIANT=w34m"
       make DESIGN_CONFIG=designs/sky130hd/sigil_hier/config.mk NUM_CORES=4 FLOW_VARIANT=t2 SIGIL_TOP_SYNTH=1 $B $FP synth
       make DESIGN_CONFIG=designs/sky130hd/sigil_hier/config.mk NUM_CORES=8 FLOW_VARIANT=t2 $B $FP finish
  3. ECO -> t2e (host_scripts/eco.sh t2e 12), after copying t2's
     results/logs/reports/objects dirs to t2e with cp -a:
       make ... NUM_CORES=12 FLOW_VARIANT=t2e $B $FP \
         RUN_SCRIPT=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/designs/sky130hd/sigil_hier/drt_eco_repair.tcl \
         RUN_LOG_NAME_STEM=5_2_route_eco SIGIL_ECO_SPEF=/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/results/sky130hd/sigil_hier/t2e/6_final.spef \
         SIGIL_NET_MAX_LEN=150 SIGIL_ECO_ROUNDS=3 run
       make ... NUM_CORES=12 FLOW_VARIANT=t2e $B $FP finish
  4. STA (host_scripts/tsta.sh t2e ~/sb/sta/top-t2e "orfs tt ss ff";
     host_scripts/bsta.sh for the blocks): per corner
       RES=<results dir> CORNER=<orfs|tt|ss|ff> OUT=<dir> PDKLIB=<dir with the
       sky130_fd_sc_hd tt/ss/ff libs> [BLOCK_LIBS="<dir>/sigil_cpu_%c.lib <dir>/sigil_crypto_top_%c.lib"] \
       openroad -exit -no_init flow/designs/sky130hd/sigil_hier/corner_sta.tcl
  5. KLayout DRC (host_scripts/sdrc.sh):
       klayout -b -rd in_gds=<t2e 6_final.gds> -rd report_file=drc.lyrdb \
         -rd exclude='sky130_sram_*' -rd tile=200 -rd threads=16 -r signoff/sky130hd_sigil.lydrc
       klayout -b -rd in_gds=platforms/sky130ram/<m>/<m>.gds -rd report_file=drc.lyrdb \
         -rd tile=100 -rd threads=10 -r signoff/sky130hd_sigil.lydrc
       python3 signoff/lyrdb_sum.py drc.lyrdb [--soc]
  6. LVS (host_scripts/mkcdl.sh, then host_scripts/hlvs.sh):
       write_cdl of each level (masters: platform sky130hd.cdl, the block
       CDLs, OpenRAM pin-only stubs); cat; signoff/cdl_drop_empty.py;
       klayout -b -rd in_gds=<6_final.gds> -rd cdl_file=concat_lvs.cdl -rd top_cell=<top> \
         -rd report_file=lvs.lvsdb -rd target_netlist=extracted.cir -rd blank='sky130_sram_1rw1r_*' \
         -rd flatten='sky130_fd_sc_hd__fill_*,sky130_fd_sc_hd__tapvpwrvgnd_*,sky130_fd_sc_hd__diode_*' \
         -r signoff/sky130hd_sigil.lylvs   (threads(4) -> threads(8))
  7. Area / pins: ODB=<6_final.odb> openroad -exit -no_init signoff/area.tcl (io.tcl);
     GDS: gzip -9 -c 6_final.gds > ~/sb/final/sigil_soc_top_sky130hd.gds.gz; sha256sum.
